---
import "../styles.css";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
const asset = (name: string): string => `${base}assets/${name}`;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="description" content="LuDash is an experimental Wayland tiling desktop built with C++20, OpenGL and Quickshell. Explore its workspace, setup guide and documentation.">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#101b1d">
  <title>LuDash — A little more room to think.</title>
  <link rel="icon" href={asset("mark.svg")} type="image/svg+xml">
  <script>import "../app";</script>
</head>
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<header class="nav wrap">
  <a class="brand" href="#" aria-label="LuDash home"><img src={asset("mark.svg")} alt="" width="28" height="28"> LuDash</a>
  <nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#workspace">Workspace</a><a href="#setup">Make it yours</a><a href={`${base}docs/settings/`}>Guides &amp; API</a><a class="source" href="https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LuDash">Source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></nav>
</header>
<main id="main">
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> WAYLAND DESKTOP · DEVELOPMENT PREVIEW 0.1</div>
    <h1>A little more<br>room to <em>think.</em></h1>
    <div class="hero-bottom"><p>A quiet panel. Windows that fall into place.<br>A Linux workspace you can make your own.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="#start">Explore LuDash <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="text-link" href={`${base}docs/start/`}>Read the field guide ↗</a></div></div>
    <figure class="desktop-frame"><div class="frame-label"><span>01 / THE WORKSPACE</span><span>C11 / C++20 + QUICKSHELL</span></div><img src={asset("desktop.png")} alt="LuDash desktop with rounded blue panel, florist wallpaper and a translucent dashboard." width="1440" height="900" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>A real LuDash session. Wallpaper included. Your windows take it from here.</figcaption></figure>
  </section>
  <div class="tech-strip"><div class="wrap"><span>WAYLAND NATIVE</span><span>OPENGL / OPENGL ES</span><span>ARCH FIRST</span><span>GPL-3.0</span></div></div>
  <section id="workspace" class="wrap section">
    <div class="section-top"><span class="eyebrow">LESS FRICTION / MORE FOCUS</span><h2>Everything has<br>its place.</h2><p>Built around a master-and-stack layout, with the controls you need close at hand.</p></div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <article class="feature"><div class="mini-tiles" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><span class="number">01</span><h3>Find your rhythm.</h3><p>Up to nine workspaces, automatic tiling and keyboard navigation. Float a window when you need a different arrangement.</p><code>Super + 1–4</code></article>
      <article class="feature"><div class="mini-panel" aria-hidden="true">◇ <span>◆ · · ·</span><b>◈ LuDash</b> ◷</div><span class="number">02</span><h3>A lighter touch.</h3><p>A rounded Quickshell panel, application launcher and real system statistics. A desktop that leaves the wallpaper room to breathe.</p><code>QML, all the way down</code></article>
      <article class="feature"><div class="mini-code" aria-hidden="true">context → shader<br><span>→ your desktop</span></div><span class="number">03</span><h3>Built in the open.</h3><p>C++20 behind the scenes. Explicit graphics contexts, vertex and fragment shaders, and metadata-based native effect plugins.</p><code>OpenGL 3.3 / GLES 3.0</code></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="setup" class="setup-section"><div class="wrap setup-grid">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">A DESKTOP THAT FEELS LIKE YOURS</span><h2>Settle in.<br>Then make it yours.</h2><p>The first-run guide helps you choose a language, check your network and shape your workspace. Existing connections carry over. You can keep going offline, too.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}docs/settings/`}>Explore configuration ↗</a><ol class="steps"><li><span>01</span>Choose your language</li><li><span>02</span>Check your connection</li><li><span>03</span>Find your colors</li><li><span>04</span>Make yourself at home</li></ol></div>
    <div class="customize"><div class="card-top"><span>PERSONALIZE / LIVE PREVIEW</span><span aria-hidden="true">⚙</span></div><div class="preview-tiles" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><h3>A small change. A different mood.</h3><p id="preview-note">Try an accent below. This changes the website preview only.</p><div class="swatches" role="group" aria-label="Preview accent color"><button data-color="#7dcccf" aria-label="Teal accent" aria-pressed="true" class="teal"></button><button data-color="#c4b5fd" aria-label="Lavender accent" aria-pressed="false" class="lavender"></button><button data-color="#e7b899" aria-label="Sand accent" aria-pressed="false" class="sand"></button><button data-color="#a8c89b" aria-label="Sage accent" aria-pressed="false" class="sage"></button></div><div class="custom-row"><label for="gap">Window gaps</label><input id="gap" type="range" min="4" max="32" value="12" step="4"><output for="gap" id="gap-value">12 px</output></div><div class="custom-footer">In LuDash: saved colors, gaps, panel height, wallpaper and information-card preferences.</div></div>
  </div></section>
  <section id="start" class="wrap section start-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">FOR THE CURIOUS</span><h2>Meet your next<br>side project.</h2><p>Start inside your current Wayland desktop. Arch Linux is the first target; the C++ backend uses portable CMake and Qt.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LuDash/blob/main/docs/TESTING_AND_FILES.md">Dependencies, testing &amp; every file ↗</a></div><div class="terminal"><div class="terminal-top"><span>ARCH LINUX / NESTED SESSION</span><button id="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre><code id="commands">git clone https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LuDash.git
cd LuDash
cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja \
  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug
cmake --build build --parallel 4
QT_QPA_PLATFORM=wayland \
  ./build/ludash-compositor --socket ludash-test</code></pre><p>Install the dependencies in the guide before building.</p><span id="copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div></section>
  <section class="wrap status-section"><span class="eyebrow">HONESTLY, STILL GROWING</span><div><h2>A working preview.<br>An open road ahead.</h2><p>LuDash is an experimental desktop, not a production-ready KDE replacement. Nested software-rendered sessions are tested locally; real GPU and standalone login sessions need broader testing.</p><p>Multiple outputs, screen locking, full portals and complete input-method integration are still ahead. Network setup uses the system's editor. Native plugins are opt-in and are not sandboxed.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LuDash/blob/main/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md">Read the current architecture ↗</a></div></section>
  <section class="wrap docs-section"><h2>Take a closer look.</h2><div class="doc-links"><a href={`${base}docs/settings/`}>Configure your desktop <span>↗</span></a><a href={`${base}docs/modules/`}>JSON &amp; QML modules <span>↗</span></a><a href={`${base}docs/api/`}>Control socket &amp; plugin API <span>↗</span></a><a href={`${base}docs/start/`}>Run &amp; test LuDash <span>↗</span></a><a href="https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LuDash/blob/main/docs/TESTING_AND_FILES.md">Testing &amp; file map <span>↗</span></a><a href="https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LuDash/blob/main/docs/CONFIGURATION.md">Setup &amp; customization <span>↗</span></a><a href="https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LuDash/blob/main/docs/PLUGINS.md">Build a plugin <span>↗</span></a><a href="https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LuDash/blob/main/docs/SECURITY_CHECKS.md">Security &amp; crash checks <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
</main>
<footer class="wrap"><a class="brand" href="#"><img src={asset("mark.svg")} alt="" width="25" height="25"> LuDash</a><span>Made for Linux. Open for exploration.</span><a href="https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LuDash">GitHub ↗</a></footer>
</body>
</html>
